            "topic": "Dimensional Analysis",
            "duration": 30,
            "summary": "### Core Concepts\nDimensional analysis is a method used to convert between different units of measurement. It is based on the principle that any physical quantity can be expressed in terms of a set of fundamental units, such as length, mass, and time.\n\nThe process of dimensional analysis involves expressing the quantity to be converted in terms of these fundamental units, and then using the conversion factors to obtain the desired unit. This is often done using the following equation:\n\n$$Q = k \\cdot x^a \\cdot y^b$$\n\nwhere $Q$ is the quantity to be converted, $k$ is a dimensionless constant, and $x$ and $y$ are the fundamental units.\n\nThe key to dimensional analysis is to ensure that the units on both sides of the equation are consistent. This can be done by using the following rules:\n\n*   The units of the quantity to be converted must be expressed in terms of the fundamental units.\n*   The conversion factors must be expressed in terms of the fundamental units.\n*   The units on both sides of the equation must be consistent.\n\n### Real-World Analogy & Story\nImagine you are planning a trip to a foreign country where they use a different system of measurement. You need to convert your height from meters to feet, but you don't know the conversion factor. You can use dimensional analysis to solve this problem.\n\nFirst, you need to express your height in terms of the fundamental units. Let's say your height is 1.75 meters. You can express this as:\n\n$$h = 1.75 \\, \\text{m}$$\n\nNext, you need to find the conversion factor from meters to feet. You can do this by using the following equation:\n\n$$1 \\, \\text{m} = 3.2808 \\, \\text{ft}$$\n\nNow, you can use dimensional analysis to convert your height from meters to feet:\n\n$$h = 1.75 \\, \\text{m} \\cdot \\frac{3.2808 \\, \\text{ft}}{1 \\, \\text{m}} = 5.7414 \\, \\text{ft}"
